<div class="centered-container w-container">
      <div class="cs-showcase-stack">
        <div class="cs-showcase cs-showcase--stacked" data-cs-video-tabs>
          <h3 class="cs-showcase__heading"><span class="cs-showcase__num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>Marketplace PDP</h3>
          <div class="cs-showcase__section-intro text-wrapper">
            <p class="subpage-title-highlight">Fixing the page most people land on</p>
            <p class="subpage-paragraph-left">Marketplace posts make up over <strong>70%</strong> of activity on the nebenan platform. The Product Detail Page (PDP) is one of the most visited surfaces on nebenan: largely driven by notifications. It’s a major engagement driver, but it desperately needed our attention: high bounce, weak continuation into the feed, and a broken share link in the user flow.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-showcase__problems cs-showcase__problems--section">
            <p class="cs-showcase__problems-lead">I was handed three identified problems:</p>
            <div class="cs-problem-cards" role="list">
              <article class="cs-problem-card outline_box red" role="listitem">
                <span class="cs-problem-card__num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
                <p class="cs-problem-card__body">Bounce rate was above&nbsp;<strong>50%</strong>.</p>
              </article>
              <article class="cs-problem-card outline_box red" role="listitem">
                <span class="cs-problem-card__num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
                <p class="cs-problem-card__body">Only&nbsp;<strong>~10%</strong> continued shopping into the main feed.</p>
              </article>
              <article class="cs-problem-card outline_box red" role="listitem">
                <span class="cs-problem-card__num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
                <p class="cs-problem-card__body">A share link or out-of-hood listing could hit a dead-end, or even a&nbsp;<strong>404</strong>.</p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-showcase__section-intro text-wrapper">
            <p class="subpage-paragraph-left">For the last point (3), I went to engineering to map every use case: deeplink for logged-out users, deeplink to a listing that no longer exists, and similar dead-ends. I designed a solution for each, so users coming via notifications stay in discovery instead of hitting a dead-end.</p>
            <p class="subpage-paragraph-left">But for the first two problem points, I needed a deeper exploration. With limited tracking, I had only a partial view of what worked and what didn’t in the current state. So I ran multiple design-thinking workshops with colleagues and qualitative user interviews.</p>
            <p class="subpage-paragraph-left"><strong>My learning:</strong> after my initial belief that optimizing cross-selling would keep users in a continuous flow, I had to see that the real pain point was somewhere else. Big cities can offer a rich Marketplace experience on nebenan, but most of Germany (lower-activity neighborhoods) quickly reaches the end of Marketplace offerings. There is nothing to cross-sell. What these neighbors really needed was wider reach: access to nearby neighborhoods for more Marketplace inventory.</p>
            <aside class="advocacy-callout advocacy-callout--selective" aria-labelledby="marketplace-judgement-title">
              <h2 id="marketplace-judgement-title" class="advocacy-callout__title type-label">My judgement in the process</h2>
              <p class="advocacy-callout__lead"><strong>During exploration, I uncovered a surprising root cause that was beyond my initiative’s scope.</strong> It needed collaboration with other teams and stakeholders. I strongly believed this would bring the real impact my project KPIs were aiming for: wider reach for Marketplace users.</p>
              <p class="advocacy-callout__lead advocacy-callout__lead--follow"><strong>So I kept focus on what was realistic within my scope, improving simpler features first, and in the meantime continued collaborating with other teams to validate the concept and bring wider reach to users later (about a year later).</strong></p>
              <p class="advocacy-callout__lead advocacy-callout__lead--follow"><strong>I designed one hypothesis (A/B test) for each of these three core problems</strong>, plus a bunch of small UX improvements to test for cumulative impact. I also used the opportunity for an overall design refresh and to optimize the information architecture.</p>
            </aside>
          </div>
          <div class="section-body friction-section cs-showcase__friction is-hidden">
            <p class="subpage-title-highlight friction-section__heading">Critical pain points:</p>
            <div class="friction-stack" data-friction-stack data-card-count="4" data-stack-label="PDP friction">
              <div class="friction-stack__shell">
                <div class="friction-stack__stage" aria-live="polite">
                  <article class="friction-stack__card outline_box red" data-friction-card="0">
                    <p class="friction-stack__text">
                      <strong class="friction-stack__title">Hard to scan</strong>
                      <span class="friction-stack__body">Information architecture made a listing harder to understand at a glance, slowing the decision and contact.</span>
                    </p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="friction-stack__card outline_box red" data-friction-card="1">
                    <p class="friction-stack__text">
                      <strong class="friction-stack__title">Weak cross-sell</strong>
                      <span class="friction-stack__body">Once someone opened a listing, there was little to keep them browsing a related item or returning to the feed.</span>
                    </p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="friction-stack__card outline_box red" data-friction-card="2">
                    <p class="friction-stack__text">
                      <strong class="friction-stack__title">Broken edge case</strong>
                      <span class="friction-stack__body">A logged-out visitor or out-of-hood listing created a dead-end. A share link sometimes failed outright.</span>
                    </p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="friction-stack__card outline_box red" data-friction-card="3">
                    <p class="friction-stack__text">
                      <strong class="friction-stack__title">Inconsistent components</strong>
                      <span class="friction-stack__body">PDP and feed items needed a flexible architecture that worked for a post, Marketplace, and event, not a one-off screen.</span>
                    </p>
                  </article>
                </div>
                <div class="friction-stack__navs">
                  <button type="button" class="friction-stack__nav friction-stack__nav--prev" aria-label="Previous friction point">
                    <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                      <path d="M14.5 5.5L8 12l6.5 6.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                    </svg>
                  </button>
                  <button type="button" class="friction-stack__nav friction-stack__nav--next" aria-label="Next friction point">
                    <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                      <path d="M9.5 5.5L16 12l-6.5 6.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                    </svg>
                  </button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-showcase__tabs" hidden>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cs-showcase__tab is-active"
              role="tab"
              aria-selected="true"
              data-cs-video-tab="pdp"
              data-video-src="/assets/case-studies/marketplace-pdp-playlist.mp4?v=1"
              data-video-label="Marketplace PDP walkthrough"
              data-previous-src="/assets/case-studies/marketplace-pdp-old.png"
              data-previous-label="Previous Marketplace PDP design"
            >Marketplace PDP</button>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-showcase__stage">
            <div class="cs-showcase__device">
              <div class="phone-mockup image-115 phone-mockup--showcase" aria-label="Marketplace PDP walkthrough on phone">
                <div class="phone-mockup__frame">
                  <div class="phone-mockup__speaker" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                  <div class="phone-mockup__video-stack" data-cs-video-stack>
                    <video
                      class="phone-mockup__video phone-mockup__video--active"
                      data-cs-video-slot="0"
                      src="/assets/case-studies/marketplace-pdp-playlist.mp4?v=1"
                      muted
                      loop
                      playsinline
                      preload="auto"
                      aria-label="Marketplace PDP walkthrough"
                    ></video>
                    <video
                      class="phone-mockup__video"
                      data-cs-video-slot="1"
                      muted
                      playsinline
                      preload="auto"
                      aria-hidden="true"
                      aria-label="Marketplace PDP walkthrough"
                    ></video>
                    <img
                      class="phone-mockup__previous"
                      data-cs-previous-img
                      alt=""
                      hidden
                    />
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <button
                type="button"
                class="cs-previous-design-btn"
                data-cs-previous-toggle
                aria-pressed="false"
              >
                <svg class="cs-previous-design-btn__icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M20.5 8.5A8 8 0 0 0 6.2 6.2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                  <path d="M5.5 3.5v3.8h3.8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                  <path d="M3.5 15.5a8 8 0 0 0 14.3 2.3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                  <path d="M18.5 20.5v-3.8h-3.8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                </svg>
                <span data-cs-previous-label>Old design</span>
              </button>
            </div>
            <aside class="cs-showcase__cards" data-cs-tab-panel="pdp" aria-label="PDP improvements">
              <p class="cs-showcase__cards-title">Improvements:</p>
              <p class="cs-showcase__cards-intro">Improving the PDP wasn’t only about polishing a listing. It was about turning notification traffic into continued Marketplace engagement: a clearer page, a safer edge case, and cross-sell that invites the next browse.</p>
              <div class="cs-card-stack" data-cs-card-stack>
                <div class="cs-card-stack__pin" data-cs-card-stack-pin>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Clearer information architecture</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">I restructured content so the listing is easy to scan. Collapsed details to save space and make sure related content falls within the fold.</p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Swipeable image gallery</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">Previously, viewing all images was only possible in a full-screen gallery with heavy performance. Now, swiping through pics quickly is easy and fast. Less friction before contacting the seller.</p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Bookmarking &amp; sharing</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">Save and share actions more in sight, more at hand.</p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Clearer CTA guidance</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">Easier path to contacting the seller: the main CTA is a sticky button, always in sight.</p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Improve cross-sell relevance</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">Previously, “additional content” below the listing was missing relevance. Now, the new swipeable galleries were aggregated from the same category and from the most popular categories.</p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Fixed the (not so) edge cases</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">Users received a deeplink, now even if they are logged-out or the listing happens to be outside of their origin neighborhood: no more dead-end, no more share-link 404s error pages.</p>
                  </article>
                </div>
              </div>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-showcase cs-showcase--stacked" data-cs-video-tabs>
          <h3 class="cs-showcase__heading"><span class="cs-showcase__num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>Monetization: Listing Boost feature</h3>
          <div class="cs-showcase__section-intro text-wrapper">
            <p class="subpage-paragraph-left">After shipping the PDP redesign, I gathered more evidence for why we should shift focus to the Feed. A growing amount of user feedback from different sources (market-fit survey, App Store, user surveys) showed the need for essential features like search. I wanted to implement Search above all else, but it got deprioritized multiple times.</p>
            <aside class="advocacy-callout" aria-label="Priority decision">
              <p class="advocacy-callout__lead">I did not freeze the initiative (implementing Search) but I continued to gather evidence to pre-validate my pitch for the search function, but I set it aside and focused on what the business needed more urgently: monetization.</p>
            </aside>
            <p class="subpage-title-highlight">From broad discovery to validation</p>
            <p class="subpage-paragraph-left">As nebenan.de had limited sources of revenue, we explored new opportunities. I ran user research with multiple, distinctive ideas on monetization. I paid careful attention to find a balance, so people get a real value for exchange. Some of the ideas were: Offering an Ad-free platform use (subscription), Crowdfunding feature to match user behavior (helping each other), Marketplace features, and many more<span class="cs-ellipsis" aria-hidden="true">...</span></p>
            <p class="subpage-paragraph-left">As in big teams and business constraints, pragmatism and incremental development, and least risky, low-effort solutions are prioritized. So we ended up shifting our focus onto the Marketplace. Why? Marketplace posts are over <strong>70%</strong> of activity: a clear commercial opportunity. Before building, I needed to know whether a neighbor would pay for better listing visibility.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-showcase__tabs" hidden>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cs-showcase__tab is-active"
              role="tab"
              aria-selected="true"
              data-cs-video-tab="boost"
              data-video-src="/assets/case-studies/marketplace-boost-feature.mp4?v=1"
              data-video-label="Boost feature walkthrough"
              data-video-crop="top"
            >Boost feature</button>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-showcase__stage">
            <div class="cs-showcase__device">
              <div class="phone-mockup image-115 phone-mockup--showcase is-crop-top" aria-label="Boost feature walkthrough on phone">
                <div class="phone-mockup__frame">
                  <div class="phone-mockup__speaker" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                  <div class="phone-mockup__video-stack" data-cs-video-stack>
                    <video
                      class="phone-mockup__video phone-mockup__video--active"
                      data-cs-video-slot="0"
                      src="/assets/case-studies/marketplace-boost-feature.mp4?v=1"
                      muted
                      loop
                      playsinline
                      preload="auto"
                      aria-label="Boost feature walkthrough"
                    ></video>
                    <video
                      class="phone-mockup__video"
                      data-cs-video-slot="1"
                      muted
                      playsinline
                      preload="auto"
                      aria-hidden="true"
                      aria-label="Boost feature walkthrough"
                    ></video>
                    <img
                      class="phone-mockup__previous"
                      data-cs-previous-img
                      alt=""
                      hidden
                    />
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <button
                type="button"
                class="cs-previous-design-btn"
                data-cs-previous-toggle
                aria-pressed="false"
                hidden
              >
                <svg class="cs-previous-design-btn__icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M20.5 8.5A8 8 0 0 0 6.2 6.2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                  <path d="M5.5 3.5v3.8h3.8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                  <path d="M3.5 15.5a8 8 0 0 0 14.3 2.3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                  <path d="M18.5 20.5v-3.8h-3.8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                </svg>
                <span data-cs-previous-label>Old design</span>
              </button>
            </div>
            <aside class="cs-showcase__cards" data-cs-tab-panel="boost" aria-label="Boost process">
              <p class="cs-showcase__cards-title">Features implemented:</p>
              <div class="cs-card-stack" data-cs-card-stack>
                <div class="cs-card-stack__pin" data-cs-card-stack-pin>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Fake door test → Boost feature MVP</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">Before investing in engineering, we set up a Fake-door test. I designed the “Boost feature” UI as real as possible and showed it to users in real context: this test showed us there is a clear interest: people are willing to pay in order to sell fast and without a hustle. Even free items converted well.<br/><br/>MVP rolled out and the result of the A/B test (on Android platform only) gave us a significant positive result: <strong>+34% units sold</strong>, revenue +4%, enough signal to scale.</p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Scaling the feature</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">From the fake door test results, demand was clear: To give users more flexibility on pricing, we iterated the Boost feature and offered multiple price packages with matching benefits. We needed to validate willingness to pay across feature combinations, but the early signs were strong enough to scale.</p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Results</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">After full-platform launch, revenue grew organically: <strong>+43.7%</strong> (<strong>€20.4k</strong>) over seven months with zero extra marketing spend.</p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Impact</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">Boost became a stable, low-maintenance revenue stream. Price testing settled at <strong>€3.49</strong>.</p>
                  </article>
                </div>
              </div>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-showcase cs-showcase--stacked" data-cs-video-tabs>
          <h3 class="cs-showcase__heading"><span class="cs-showcase__num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>Marketplace Feed</h3>
          <div class="cs-showcase__section-intro text-wrapper">
            <p class="subpage-paragraph-left">The time had come for iteration 2.0, and I returned to my earlier initiative: implementing the essentials of the Marketplace feed, Search, saved Search, and improved filters. And the fruit of a company wide collaboration: wider reach for Marketplace users. </p>
            <p class="subpage-paragraph-left">My pre-validation was backed by user feedback and benchmarking against industry standards.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-showcase__tabs" hidden>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cs-showcase__tab is-active"
              role="tab"
              aria-selected="true"
              data-cs-video-tab="feed"
              data-video-src="/assets/case-studies/marketplace-feed-playlist.mp4?v=4"
              data-video-label="Marketplace Feed walkthrough"
            >Marketplace Feed</button>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-showcase__stage">
            <div class="cs-showcase__device">
              <div class="phone-mockup image-115 phone-mockup--showcase" aria-label="Marketplace Feed walkthrough on phone">
                <div class="phone-mockup__frame">
                  <div class="phone-mockup__speaker" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                  <div class="phone-mockup__video-stack" data-cs-video-stack>
                    <video
                      class="phone-mockup__video phone-mockup__video--active"
                      data-cs-video-slot="0"
                      src="/assets/case-studies/marketplace-feed-playlist.mp4?v=4"
                      muted
                      loop
                      playsinline
                      preload="auto"
                      aria-label="Marketplace Feed walkthrough"
                    ></video>
                    <video
                      class="phone-mockup__video"
                      data-cs-video-slot="1"
                      muted
                      playsinline
                      preload="auto"
                      aria-hidden="true"
                      aria-label="Marketplace Feed walkthrough"
                    ></video>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <aside class="cs-showcase__cards" data-cs-tab-panel="feed" aria-label="Feed improvements">
              <p class="cs-showcase__cards-title">Improvements: Features implemented</p>
              <div class="cs-card-stack" data-cs-card-stack>
                <div class="cs-card-stack__pin" data-cs-card-stack-pin>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Search</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">Keyword search was missing, users had a hard time finding anything specific without endless scrolling. Compromises had to be made: smart search, auto-suggest, popular search… were all add-ons we had to postpone and keep our focus: delivering the basics first.</p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Saved search</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">Observing user behaviour outside of the marketplace made it clear: users keep looking for objects and they often did that directly on the neighborhood Feed, asking in a regular post. To help neighbors find what they want, we developed a feature to save their marketplace searches (category or search term) and get notifications if a new item appears, which directly moves our main KPIs: more successful seller contacts, more return visits.</p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Collapsed filters</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">The previous category Filter system was a poor substitute for the lack of a solid search function. Now, with that being solved, I could rethink the Categories and focus on my favourite UX pattern: Progressive disclosure. I made the filters collapsible to keep the user focus on the feed.</p>
                  </article>
                  <article class="cs-improve-card cs-card-stack__card outline_box green" data-cs-card-stack-item>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__title">Extended reach</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__body">There was a long-standing problem I knew from user complaints: In many remote regions, users did not get to see enough marketplace items, so they wished for a wider reach. This was part of a company-wide effort to give low-activity neighborhoods the option to widen their reach. As part of that initiative, we enabled this feature on the Marketplace as well, which brought a clear benefit &amp; win.</p>
                    <p class="cs-improve-card__highlight">
                      <strong>A/B test:</strong> variant won: 
                      <strong class="iteration-test__delta iteration-test__delta--win">+3.2% PDP views</strong>
                      per session and
                      <strong class="iteration-test__delta iteration-test__delta--win">+12.3% seller contacts</strong>,
                      both statistically significant.
                    </p>
                  </article>
                </div>
              </div>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section-body iteration-section iteration-learnings cs-learnings">
        <div class="text-wrapper">
          <h2 class="highlight_body subtitle-uppercase subtitle-uppercase-mobile">Takeaways</h2>
          <p class="section-title section-title-mobile">What did I learn?</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="iteration-learnings__list">
          <li>
            <strong>As a UX designer, my main mission is to advocate for the user.</strong> So I approached monetization carefully and collected feedback early. Early interviews were misleading though, and my initial hypothesis was wrong: at scale, people don’t mind paying for a Marketplace feature. The loudest pushback came from a group who use nebenan less for Marketplace and more for neighbourly help. A fake-door test was the right method: large-scale feedback, in context, in the real user flow, with the right segment (Marketplace users). In the end we found a balance that helps users sell faster and grows business revenue.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>When initiatives get deprioritized, I learned not to take it as a rejection, but as a win:</strong> more time for continuous research and pre-validation, so I can keep pitching for what I believe in.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="subpage-title-highlight cs-learnings__fact-label">Interesting finding:</p>
        <p class="subpage-paragraph-left">To my surprise, people bought Boost even for free Marketplace items, but the data didn’t show why. Qualitative interviews did: giving away free items often meant endless messaging and no-shows, lots of interest, fewer reliable pickups. Boost helped them get rid of stuff faster, with less hustle.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

